(>> 4.1 Foundations of NumPy and the ndarray Architecture) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(NumPy \(Numerical Python\) is the foundational scientific library powering Python's) Tj
T*
(engineering ecosystem:) Tj
T*
(* Limitations of Standard Python Lists: Dynamic type pointers stored across) Tj
T*
(fragmented memory locations; element-by-element loops incur massive interpreter) Tj
T*
(dispatch overhead.) Tj
T*
(* The ndarray Object: Homogeneous, fixed-size multidimensional array stored in) Tj
T*
(contiguous C-order or Fortran-order memory blocks. Supports Vectorization \(pushing) Tj
T*
(execution down to pre-compiled SIMD machine instructions\).) Tj
T*
(* Core Attributes: arr.shape \(tuple of dimensions\), arr.ndim \(number of axes\),) Tj
T*
(arr.dtype \(data type, e.g. int32, float64, complex128\), arr.size \(total element) Tj
T*
(count\), arr.itemsize \(bytes per element\).) Tj
T*
(* Array Creation Functions: np.array\(list\), np.zeros\(shape\), np.ones\(shape\),) Tj
T*
(np.full\(shape, val\), np.eye\(N\) \(identity matrix\), np.arange\(start, stop, step\),) Tj
T*
(np.linspace\(start, stop, num\) \(uniform linearly spaced intervals\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 4.2 Array Indexing, Slicing and Boolean Masking) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Multi-Dimensional Indexing: arr[row, col] \(faster than arr[row][col] which creates) Tj
T*
(intermediate list objects\).) Tj
T*
(* Slicing: arr[row_start:row_stop, col_start:col_stop]. Slices return Views \(shallow) Tj
T*
(references sharing underlying memory buffer\), not copies! Modifying a slice mutates) Tj
T*
(the original array.) Tj
T*
(* Fancy Indexing: Passing arrays of integer indices to select elements in arbitrary) Tj
T*
(non-contiguous orders.) Tj
T*
(* Boolean Masking: Applying relational expressions on arrays generates a boolean) Tj
T*
(mask: mask = \(arr > threshold\). Indexing with mask \(arr[mask]\) extracts elements) Tj
T*
(satisfying criteria in a single vectorized sweep.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 4.3 Vectorized Mathematics and Universal Functions \(ufuncs\)) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Universal Functions: Functions operating element-wise on ndarrays: np.sin\(\),) Tj
T*
(np.cos\(\), np.exp\(\), np.log\(\), np.sqrt\(\), np.abs\(\).) Tj
T*
(* Aggregation Functions: np.sum\(arr, axis\), np.mean\(\), np.std\(\), np.var\(\), np.min\(\),) Tj
T*
(np.max\(\), np.argmin\(\), np.argmax\(\).) Tj
